{"requirements":[{"id":"destination-ready","requirement":"Install a supported MariaDB on Ubuntu 24.04 node2 and leave the migrated legacy_shop database ready for use.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 runs Ubuntu-packaged MariaDB 10.11.14 with the service active and enabled. After reboot it accepted SQL, passed integrity checks, retained the database, and completed a transactional write followed by rollback.","evidence_ids":["cmd-db083ee4d30f45e4","cmd-01caa747effc4f81","cmd-39fbba96e55848ba","cmd-9a94313ffa814470","cmd-c99a9a56b9cc480a"]},{"id":"structure-preserved","requirement":"Preserve the database schema, relationships, indexes, and constraints.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Source and destination fingerprints match for tables, columns, indexes, and constraints, with identical counts of 4 tables, 23 columns, 9 indexes, 9 constraints, and 2 foreign keys. The source had no triggers, routines, events, or views requiring migration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dda1d6d92a75461e","cmd-512e96c807ea4a4e","cmd-a4b9ec977c664129"]},{"id":"data-preserved","requirement":"Preserve all legacy_shop data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Canonical hashes match between source and destination for all four tables, as do row counts, monetary totals, and zero-orphan relationship checks. The destination retained identical hashes and counts after reboot and all tables passed integrity checks.","evidence_ids":["source-row-counts","source-content-digests","cmd-8c5e279397a84ab5","cmd-040e08df47224b79","cmd-9a94313ffa814470"]},{"id":"source-unchanged","requirement":"Leave the source legacy_shop database and MariaDB service unchanged.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 remained on MariaDB 10.0.38 with its service active and its original table counts and content hashes intact. Following the mandatory restart, the same version, data, and healthy tables recovered, and migration artifacts were removed.","evidence_ids":["source-service-state","source-content-digests","cmd-b6dbf311a17e4b67","cmd-51320c9b027145d2","cmd-bb1cba6b5bd94a33"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation and index refresh were necessary prerequisites; dump creation, import, and the temporary transfer listener directly supported migration; reboot actions fulfilled the provider protocol; the write test was rolled back; and temporary files were removed. The only hygiene concern is that the database dump was briefly served over unauthenticated HTTP on node1's managed-network address. It was used for the transfer, then stopped and fully cleaned, so no exposure or residue remained. Final snapshots show healthy package state, no failed services, no migration files, and MariaDB listening only on node2 loopback.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d9215ee6febf4e6d","cmd-4d880f051a754260","cmd-13d45ead9224483b","cmd-fd01f536e3fe4cf3","cmd-bb1cba6b5bd94a33","cmd-c99a9a56b9cc480a","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material migration outcomes are satisfied with direct source/destination comparisons and post-reboot verification. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity confirmed by executor and lifecycle observations, and recovered service and data state.","limitations":["No remote application-client connection test was captured; destination readiness is demonstrated through local SQL, service health, transactional write/rollback, integrity checks, and reboot recovery.","The evidence does not establish whether the network carrying the brief unauthenticated HTTP dump transfer was otherwise isolated."]}
